## DIFC Rules of the Court — RDC 38.7 (indemnity-basis costs review)
##
## Source: Rules of the DIFC Courts, RDC 38.7. Where the court orders
## costs on the *indemnity basis*, the proportionality limb of the
## standard-basis assessment is stripped: only **reasonableness** of the
## sum claimed remains, and any doubt is resolved in favour of the
## receiving party (the inverse of the standard-basis convention).
##
## The structure of the review is:
##
##   1. The court walks each defendant's *named objection* and triages
##      it into one of four buckets:
##        Mechanically_disposed    — no specific line item named;
##                                   the objection cannot move the sum.
##        Held_to_zero             — held to zero on evidence (e.g.
##                                   line item is unsupported).
##        Deterministic_reduction  — named amount reduced by named amount.
##        Requires_human_judgment  — proportionality-style argument that
##                                   does not fall through the
##                                   reasonableness gate alone.
##
##   2. The award is the original claim minus the deterministic
##      reductions and the held-to-zero items. The *residue* is the sum
##      that would only be reachable through human judgment.
##
## Used in:
##   trace-03 — ENF 271/2025 *Taylor v Yao Affi* (Cooke J).
##
## This rule is the canonical *bounded-discretion* shape: the predicate
## says exactly what it can decide and exactly what it cannot.

```catala
declaration enumeration ObjectionBucket:
  -- Mechanically_disposed
  -- Held_to_zero
  -- Deterministic_reduction
  -- Requires_human_judgment

declaration structure Objection:
  data objection_no content integer
  data bucket content ObjectionBucket
  data named_amount_aed content decimal

declaration structure IndemnityReview:
  data claim_aed content decimal
  data mechanically_disposed_aed content decimal
  data held_to_zero_aed content decimal
  data deterministic_reductions_aed content decimal
  data residual_lower_aed content decimal
  data residual_upper_aed content decimal
  data requires_human_judgment content boolean

declaration scope IndemnityBasisReview:
  input claim_aed content decimal
  input objections content list of Objection
  output review content IndemnityReview

scope IndemnityBasisReview:
  definition review equals
    let mech equals
      sum decimal of (map each o among objections
                      such that o.bucket = Mechanically_disposed
                      to o.named_amount_aed)
    in
    let zero equals
      sum decimal of (map each o among objections
                      such that o.bucket = Held_to_zero
                      to o.named_amount_aed)
    in
    let det equals
      sum decimal of (map each o among objections
                      such that o.bucket = Deterministic_reduction
                      to o.named_amount_aed)
    in
    let human equals
      (number of (list of o among objections
                  such that o.bucket = Requires_human_judgment)) > 0
    in
    let upper equals claim_aed - zero - det in
    ## Lower bound is the same upper bound *if* no human-judgment
    ## objections were raised — the rule has nothing more to subtract.
    let lower equals
      if human then 0.00 else upper
    in
    IndemnityReview {
      -- claim_aed: claim_aed
      -- mechanically_disposed_aed: mech
      -- held_to_zero_aed: zero
      -- deterministic_reductions_aed: det
      -- residual_lower_aed: lower
      -- residual_upper_aed: upper
      -- requires_human_judgment: human
    }
```

## Test — replays trace-03's headline disposition.

```catala
#[test] declaration scope TestRDC38_7Taylor:
  composite scope IndemnityBasisReview
  output review content IndemnityReview

scope TestRDC38_7Taylor:
  definition review equals composite.review
  ## Claim AED 128,914.80; objections from Taylor v Yao Affi:
  ## (1) generic "fees too high" — mechanically disposed.
  ## (2) duplicated paralegal hours — held to zero AED 0.
  ## (3) excess senior associate time — proportionality-style,
  ##     requires human judgment.
  definition composite.claim_aed equals 128914.80
  definition composite.objections equals [
    Objection { -- objection_no: 1 -- bucket: Mechanically_disposed   -- named_amount_aed: 0.00 };
    Objection { -- objection_no: 2 -- bucket: Held_to_zero            -- named_amount_aed: 0.00 };
    Objection { -- objection_no: 3 -- bucket: Requires_human_judgment -- named_amount_aed: 0.00 }
  ]
  ## Cooke J reduced AED 128,914.80 → AED 120,000 — a residue of
  ## AED 8,914.80 (≈6.92%) reachable only through human judgment.
  assertion review.requires_human_judgment = true
  assertion review.residual_upper_aed = 128914.80
  assertion review.residual_lower_aed = 0.00
```
